From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000103 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:12:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: TF_DS_DRAFT_DEPTH2=1 pins every head draft to 2 (a
 benchmark switch)

The round loop prices each draft from the load-time table and the rounds it
measures (core/lanes/depth.zig's Rule), and T25 calibrates a stream's realised
survival into that price. That makes a depth curve hard to read: the depth a
round drafts is whatever the rule decides, not the depth under test.

This adds a benchmark pin: with TF_DS_DRAFT_DEPTH2=1 every head draft a round
asks for is 2, whatever the rule prices, in the first round after a prompt
(openDepth) and in every later one (headDepth, budgets), and the round's window
verifies 2 of them (windows.allocate) instead of trimming them by chance and
cost. Copies, forced rows and a finished stream are unchanged; the checkpoint's
own draft count and the stream's room clamp the pin. Greedy replies keep their
bits (a pinned draft is verified by the same accept/reject path); a sampled
stream's draws can differ.

Off unless set. The next patches add the 3, 4 and 5 toggles; at most one may be
on, and two at once refuse the start (error.BadDraftPin).
